{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix-forward pushed: change 1733 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1733\n(commit 8fd5166a7b, on current main d2dea317ec).\n\nVerification of the exact pushed tree:\n- main tier: 12841 passed, 52 skipped, 1 failed.\n- integration tier: 194 passed, 1 skipped.\n- ruff, mypy (526 files), complexity ratchet unchanged.\n\nThe single main-tier failure is `test_no_src_module_over_the_hard_cap` — the\n`_config_schema.py` 808-vs-800 breach, which is the OTHER session's work and which my change\ndoes not touch. I did not take that on faith: I created a throwaway worktree at pristine\nFETCH_HEAD, with none of my changes present, and ran the module-size contract there. It fails\nidentically (1 failed, 3 passed). So the breach is inherited from main, not introduced by me,\nand my change is green on everything it is responsible for.\n\nConsequence to expect: 1733 will likely take a Verified -1 for that same inherited failure,\nbecause CI tests the patchset's tree and that tree contains main's breach. That is NOT a reason\nto recheck — a recheck re-runs the same deterministic gate against the same broken file. The\nunblocking event is the other session's fix landing; then I rebase 1733 over it and CI goes\ngreen. I will not touch `_config_schema.py` to unblock myself, because two sessions editing one\nfile to satisfy one cap is how you get the collision that caused this in the first place.\n\nWhat 1733 fixes, all four live on main right now:\n1. `run_sweep` stamping the sweep clock on a stand-aside — the hole through the floor.\n2. `| tee` under pipefail masking rebar's exit code and defeating the exit-2-vs-1 branching.\n3. No test that a dry run leaves the clock unset while a real sweep sets it.\n4. The stale `close_ticket` comment claiming compaction is not triggered here and naming a\n   \"DEDICATED CLONE\"."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786645928083500001,"uuid":"c46813e2-dbd3-494e-a64a-9d909972298b"}